# Final tables — 'In which domain do the majority of authors tend to be male for both original and replication studies?'

Unit of analysis = one original–replication pair (id). Male share is taken from the supplied `authors_male.o/.r` ratios × `n_authors.o/.r`; no name-based gender inference, no modelling, no use of `replicated`/`relative_es`.

PRIMARY metric = pooled author-level male share = Σ(ratio·n_authors)/Σ(n_authors) within a domain; threshold strictly > 0.5 on BOTH sides; ratio == 0.5 counted as a tie (no majority).


